  "notes": "Official cause_code/category left TBD/provisional per FORM-366 fields (no block-13 rows provided). Narrative attributes root cause to crud accumulation on new CRDM internals prior to passivation-layer formation; theme captures this though category is provisional pending official codification. Post-event review determined the event was NOT reportable under 10 CFR 50.73(a)(2)(ii) since UFSAR Ch.15 dropped-rod analysis bounds the condition -- captured via rr_5073ii edge and rr_ufsar15 node, though this criterion was ultimately not applicable per licensee determination. No previous similar occurrence reported (explicitly stated none in past three years), so no stub LER/SIMILAR_TO edge emitted. RPV (reactor vessel head) node reflects the recently replaced component context tied to CRDM installation age, not a failure participant per se; retained as Component given explicit narrative linkage to CRDM replacement project causing the immature passivation layer condition."
